On November 2 2008, Sierra/Vivendi disabled the authentication servers
required for TRIBES 2 online multiplayer.
Since January 2009, TribesNEXT provides a new multiplayer account system
and master server, safely connecting tens of thousands of Tribes players around the world.
TribesNEXT is unfortunately only available as a Windows patch.

**********************************************
* TribesNEXT for Loki's Tribes 2 build 25034 *
**********************************************

Features:
- use TribesNext_rc2a.exe Windows patch as base
- use an LD_PRELOAD shim with 'tribes2.dynamic', works on modern Linux system (SDL3, Wayland, ...)
- fixed strcmp.cs
- public.store & private.store are stored in ~/.loki/tribes2/


Requirements:
- Loki's Tribes 2 install, updated to build 25034 (tribes2-25034-cdrom-x86.run)
- Follow instructions from https://github.com/twolife/tribes2-linux-sdl
  to be able to play the game offline.


Install:
- copy the 'tribesnext' directory to the game directory
- Optional (you can use the pre-build object): build the C shim code.
- copy c_shim/libtribesnext.so to your game directory
- run 'bash install.sh patch'

Howto run game:
  LD_PRELOAD=./libstdc++-3-libc6.2-2-2.10.0.so:./tribes2shim.so:./libtribesnext.so ./tribes2.dynamic -online


Uninstall:
- run 'bash install.sh unpatch'
- remove libtribesnext.so from the game directory


Credits/Thanks:
  Many thanks to "calvin_balke" for his initial work more than a decade ago:
  - https://tribesnext.com/forum/discussion/3329/tribesnext-patch-for-loki-port-on-linux
  - https://dl.dropbox.com/s/g02o5oa2d1gecnk/t2patch.tar
  This was really helpful, I wouldn't have sorted this out so quickly if I had started from scratch.
